paths: file:v1/runtime/backend/js/src/main/resources/scalascript/js-runtime/core-dispatch.mjs file:v1/runtime/backend/js/BUGS.md file:tests/conformance/long-overflow-wrap.ssc file:tests/conformance/expected/long-overflow-wrap.txt file:v1/runtime/backend/js/src/main/scala/scalascript/codegen/JsGen.scala file:bench/history.tsv
scope: |
  `_arith`'s bigint branch returns unmasked BigInt for + - * / %, so ssc Long does not wrap at
  64 bits on the JS lane: it diverges from INT/JVM AND grows without bound. Measured on the
  bench corpus LCG (tuple-monoid): 6,131,220-bit `s` and 43.5 s per pass vs 64 bits and 5 ms
  masked. Fix = BigInt.asIntN(64, …) on the arithmetic ops (`_bit` already does this), gated by
  a new lane-independent conformance case with a golden.
  Widened again 2026-07-31: the mask CANNOT live in the shared `_arith` — ssc `BigInt` is the
  same JS representation and must stay unbounded (measured: BigInt(1e9)^4 truncated). It goes in a
  new `_larith` that only JsGen's `isLongExpr` guard emits, so JsGen.scala is now in scope.
  Widened 2026-07-31: the case is named `long-overflow-wrap` (not `js-…`) because it runs on
  every lane. The roster/baseline freeze is NOT in scope — `v2-char-value` holds those two files
  and is adding a case of its own; whoever refreshes the freeze last covers both cases.
next: implement + gate, then re-run bench.sh (its js column measured the bug)
